# Server-side configuration for the /api/schedules proxy.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local use with `vercel dev`, and set the same names in
# Vercel under Project Settings -> Environment Variables for deployments.
#
# Neither name is prefixed VITE_, and that is deliberate: Vite only inlines
# VITE_* into the client bundle, so these cannot leak into the JavaScript the
# browser downloads. Do not rename them with a VITE_ prefix.

# Origin of the Tripket schedules API, no trailing path. Must be https for any
# public host; the proxy refuses plaintext http unless the host is localhost,
# 127.0.0.1, *.test or *.local, so a dev box still works.
#
# The snippet from the developer used http://api.tripket.test, which is a
# machine-local hostname — it does not resolve from Vercel, so a real public
# origin is needed before the section shows anything in production.
TRIPKET_API_BASE=https://api.tripketph.com

# Optional. Sent to the upstream as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Leave
# unset if the endpoint is public. This is a secret: it stays on the server and
# is never returned to the browser.
# TRIPKET_API_TOKEN=
